{"id":"word:hebrew:H389","type":"word","title":"אַךְ","subtitle":"H389 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a particle of affirmation , surely ; hence (by limitation) only","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אַךְ (H389) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 161 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אַךְ (ʼak) means a particle of affirmation , surely ; hence (by limitation) only First listed occurrence: 1Chr 22 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אַךְ","transliteration":"ʼak","pronunciation":"ak","strong":"H389","lemmaId":"hebrew:H389","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["אַךְ","אַ֣ךְ","אַ֥ךְ","אַ֚ךְ","אַ֤ךְ"],"morphs":[["HTa",158],["HC/D",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"a particle of affirmation , surely ; hence (by limitation) only","usage":"also, in any wise, at least, but, certainly, even, howbeit, nevertheless, notwithstanding, only, save, surely, of a surety, truly, verily, wherefore, yet (but).","full":"H389. ak אַךְ 159 adverb (perhaps from the same demonstr, root found also in כֵּן כֹּה, כִּי, ). 1 surely . 2 with a restrictive force, emphasizing what follows : a. in contrast to what precedes, howbeit ; b. in contrast with other ideas Generally , only 1 asseverative, often introducing with emphasis the expression of a truth (or supposed truth) newly perceived, especially in colloquial language, surely, no doubt (doch wohl) ; Gen 26:9 הִוא אִשְׁתְּךָ הִנֵּה אַךְ of a surety , lo, she is thy wife ! 29:14 ; 44:28 ; Judg 3:24 ; 20:39 ; 1Sam 16:6 surely the anointed of ׳י is before him ! 25:21 ; Jer 5:4 ; Psalm 58:12; Psa 73:1 ; 73:13 ; but also in other cases, though rarely, Isa 34:14-15 , Zeph 3:7 ; Psa 23:6 ; 139:11 ; Psalm 140:14; Job 16:7 ; 18:21 ; & rather singularly Exod 12:15 ; 31:13 ; Lev 23:27 , 39 (all P). 2 restrictive : a. in contrast to what precedes , howbeit, yet, but : Gen 9:4 howbeit , flesh with the life thereof . . . ye shall not eat, 20:12 ; Exod 21:21 ; Lev 21:23 ; 27:26 ; Num 18:15 , 17 ; 2Sam 3:13 ; Jer 10:24 correct me, בְּמִשְׁמָּט אַךְ but with judgment, Job 2:6 ; 13:15 ; sometimes with an adversative force, as Isa 14:15 ; 43:24 ; before an imperative (minimizing the request), Gen 23:13 only , if thou wilt, I pray thee, hear me ! 27:13 ; Judg 10:15 ; 1Sam 18:17 ; 1Kin 17:13 and elsewhere So 1Sam 8:9 כִּי אַךְ (see כִּי ; and compare πλὴν ὅτι ). b. in contrast to other ideas Generally : — ( α ) Gen 7:23 ; 18:32 הַמַּעַם אַךְ only this once (so Exod 10:17 and elsewhere) 34:15 ; 12:16 (note accents), 1Sam 18:8 תַמְּלוּכָה אַךְ לוֺ וְעוֺד and there yet remains for him only the kingdom, 21:5 ; Isa 45:14 אֵל בְּךָ אַךָ only in thee is God! Psa 62:2 etc. Job 14:22 ; Psa 37:8 fret not thyself לְהָרֵעַ אַךְ (which leadeth) only to do evil, Prov 11:24 he that withholdeth more than is meet לְמַחְסוֺר אַךְ (tendeth) only to penury, 14:23 ; 21:5 ; 22:16 ; ( β ) attaching itself closely to the following word (usually an adjective, rarely a verb), only , i.e. exclusively, altogether, utterly Deut 16:15 and thou shalt be שָׂמֵחַ אַךְ altogether rejoicing, 28:29 (compare 28:33 רַק ) Isa 16:7 נְכָאִים אַךְ utterly stricken, 19:11 ; Jer 16:19 nought but lies, 32:30 ; Hosea 12:12 ; Job 19:13 זָרוּ אַךְ are wholly estranged (with play on אַכְזָר cruel ). c. as an adverb of time (with infinitive absolute), twice: Gen 27:30 בָּא יַעֲקֹבוְ֗֗֗עֵשָׂו יָצָא יָצאֹ אַךְ only just (or scarcely ) had Jacob gone out, . . . and (= when) Esau came in, Judg 7:19 . &#8212; וְאַח thrice : Gen 9:5 and only (second limitation of 9:3 ); Num 22:20 but only ; Josh 22:19 but howbeit. Note. — In some passages the affirmative and restrictive senses agree equally with the context; and authorities read the Hebrew differently. Thus only = nought but, altogether , is adopted by Ges Ew Hi De in Psa 23:6 ; 62:10 ; 73:1 ; 73:13 ; by Ew Hi De in 39:6 ; 39:7 (Che surely ); by Ges Ew De in 39:12 (but Hi Che surely ); by Ew Hi in 73:18 (De Che surely ); by Ges Hi De in 139:11 (Ew doch ). Isa 45:14 Ges Ew Hi Di only ; but De Che of a truth .","rootNote":"akin to 403 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 22 12","keyReferences":["1Chr 22 12","1Kgs 9 24","1Kgs 11 12","1Kgs 11 39","1Kgs 17 13","1Kgs 22 32","1Kgs 22 44","1Sam 1 23"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":161,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 22 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֣ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 9 24","book":"1Kgs","chapter":9,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֣ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 12","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 39","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֖ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 17 13","book":"1Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֣ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 32","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":32,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֣ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 44","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":44,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֥ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 23","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֛ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 8 9","book":"1Sam","chapter":8,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֗ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 12 20","book":"1Sam","chapter":12,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֗ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 12 24","book":"1Sam","chapter":12,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַ֣ךְ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTa"},{"reference":"1Sam 16 6","book":"1Sa